Derived structure
-----------------
The specification format (holes filled by a solver, frozen correctness and cost theorems,
ChallengeJson files), the module layout and the imports of every file in QuantumSpecs/ and
QuantumSolutions/ follow formal-quantum-computation. The specifications and solutions use its
QuantumComputation library and, where noted below, its QuantumComputationSpecs and
QuantumComputationDiscoveries libraries. Those libraries are not copied here; Lake fetches
them from the repository above at the commit pinned in lakefile.toml and lake-manifest.json.

Every specification and most solutions contain the documentation sentence "By default we allow
only a single variable.", taken from QuantumComputationSpecs/Primitives/Arcsin.lean.

