Lower bounds
------------
LowerBounds/Grover/Statement.lean has the line "Portions Copyright 2026 Google LLC (marked
GOOGLE-DERIVED below)" in its header. Between the markers BEGIN GOOGLE-DERIVED and END
GOOGLE-DERIVED it restates, at m = k = 1, the program construction of groverFindAnyProgram, the
postcondition of groverFindAny_correctness and the cost predicate of groverFindAny_rel_cost from
QuantumComputationSpecs/Algorithms/Grover.lean (Copyright 2026 Google LLC), with the circuit and
its qubit count quantified instead of fixed.

LowerBounds/Grover/RelCostStatement.lean has the same header line. Between its two pairs of
markers it restates the types of the four definition holes of the find-any challenge, the program
construction of groverFindAnyProgram, and the statements of groverFindAny_correctness and
groverFindAny_rel_cost from QuantumComputationSpecs/Algorithms/Grover.lean (Copyright 2026 Google
LLC), with each hole replaced by a field of a structure.

LowerBounds/Grover/ParallelStatement.lean has the same header line. Between its markers it
restates, for any number m of oracle slots and k of marked items, the program construction shared
by groverFindAnyProgram and groverFindAllProgram, the postconditions of groverFindAny_correctness
and groverFindAll_correctness and the cost predicate of groverFindAny_rel_cost and
groverFindAll_rel_cost from QuantumComputationSpecs/Algorithms/Grover.lean (Copyright 2026 Google
LLC), with the circuit and its qubit count quantified instead of fixed.

LowerBounds/Grover/ParallelRelCostStatement.lean has the same header line. Between its three pairs
of markers it restates the types of the four definition holes of the find-any and find-all
challenges, the program construction of groverFindAnyProgram and groverFindAllProgram, and the
statements of groverFindAny_correctness, groverFindAny_rel_cost, groverFindAll_correctness and
groverFindAll_rel_cost from QuantumComputationSpecs/Algorithms/Grover.lean (Copyright 2026 Google
LLC), with each hole replaced by a field of a structure.

The other files in LowerBounds/, including the find-all files LowerBounds/Grover/FindAll*.lean,
copy no Google text. Lines.lean, FindAllBlockPoly.lean, FindAllJohnson.lean,
FindAllJohnsonPotential.lean, FindAllJohnsonPotentialValue.lean and FindAllTrace.lean import only
Mathlib, directly or through each other. All the others import Google's QuantumComputation and
QuantumComputationSpecs libraries, directly or through other files in LowerBounds/, and use their
definitions unmodified.
